{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":725,"final_message_hash":"sha256:d110cb1bb7f733ffa5cdd187d3ca69a25831c9878c5f8bb0edf76f413afa2060","final_message_inline":"The vendor bump to slugify 2.0.0 changed the API: the second argument became an options object, the default separator became `_`, and lowercasing became opt-in. `src/pages.ts` was still passing the 1.x string separator, so `\"-\"` was ignored and every slug came back underscore-separated and non-lowercased.\n\nFix in `src/pages.ts:11` — call the 2.0 API with the old behaviour pinned:\n\n```ts\nreturn slugify(title, { separator: \"-\", lower: true });\n```\n\nVerified:\n- `node --test` → `# pass 2`, `# fail 0`\n- `pageSlug(\"Q3 Review: Plans & Budgets (Draft)\")` → `q3-review-plans-budgets-draft`\n- `vendor/` untouched, per the repo's \"never patch a vendored file in place\" rule\n- `saga gate check` → ALL MET (G1, G2, G3)\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:6f8b1250efba13f3a78810f6d6b01cff4071565531137288dad13f3e535fe1db","hook_ms":2,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":28757556500,"prev":"sha256:ef3c3327cc9b4d65e97220aea7cd5a189156ef009ead12b11b3ab99dcae6dc24","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":25,"session":"090aa593-3790-43ab-9572-dd5bbff58da5","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T06:44:57.994Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
